{
  "contract": "Repair solve(data), an originally authored bounded event-inbox worker. The input is {'events': [event, ...]}. Every event has exactly tenant_id, event_id, and payload. All are strings; IDs are nonempty, at most 80 characters, case-sensitive, and may contain delimiters or Unicode. payload may be empty and is at most 80 characters. There are at most 32 events. These shape and size conditions are guaranteed; malformed data validation is outside this task.\nReturn a list of complete event objects in their first-occurrence input order. Identity is the pair (tenant_id, event_id), with exact string equality. Distinct pairs must remain distinct even if IDs or payloads happen to match. If a pair occurs again with the identical payload, ignore that replay. If any pair occurs again with a different payload, raise ValueError for the entire input; do not silently keep the first, replace it with the last, or return a partial result. Preserve all three fields without normalization. The host copies the input and retains the frozen original.\nThe supplied public examples currently pass and do not establish correctness. Construct valid regression inputs from this contract, state the expected result, reproduce an actual failure before repair, then rerun the same regression case on the final code and check public examples. Provide a short visible diagnosis based on recorded observations. No reference answer or private example is supplied to the acting model. This is a deliberately bounded task; it is not a claim about a real company's event system.\n",
  "control_codes": {
    "event_id_only": "def solve(data):\n    seen = set()\n    accepted = []\n    for event in data['events']:\n        key = event['event_id']\n        if key not in seen:\n            seen.add(key)\n            accepted.append(event)\n    return accepted\n",
    "ignore_payload_conflict": "def solve(data):\n    seen = set()\n    accepted = []\n    for event in data['events']:\n        key = (event['tenant_id'], event['event_id'])\n        if key not in seen:\n            seen.add(key)\n            accepted.append(event)\n    return accepted\n",
    "last_wins": "def solve(data):\n    stored = {}\n    for event in data['events']:\n        stored[(event['tenant_id'], event['event_id'])] = event\n    return list(stored.values())\n"
  },
  "family_id": "repair-scoped-event-regression",
  "initial": "def solve(data):\n    seen = {}\n    accepted = []\n    for event in data['events']:\n        key = event['tenant_id'] + ':' + event['event_id']\n        if key in seen:\n            if seen[key] != event['payload']:\n                raise ValueError('conflicting_replay')\n        else:\n            seen[key] = event['payload']\n            accepted.append(event)\n    return accepted\n",
